hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"150","Allāhumma ighfir lī warḥamnī wa alḥiqnī bir-Rafīqi'l-A'lā. O Allah, forgive me, have mercy on me, and join me with the Highest Companion (i.e., the Prophet Muhammad ﷺ in Paradise)."
"151","Jaʿala al-nabiyyu ṣallā Allāhu ʿalayhi wa-sallam ʿinda mawtihi yadkhulu yadayhi fī al-māʾ fa-yamsaḥu bihimā wajhahu wa-yaqūl: Lā ilāha illā Allāna, inna lil-mawti la-sakarāt.. The Prophet (peace be upon him) at the time of his death, he put his hands in the water and wiped his face with them and said: \There is no god but God"," verily for death there are moments of agony.\"""""
